module

public import Theory.Representation.BinaryNaturalDual.ModelOrbits.AutomorphismModel.Action

/-!
# The actual binary natural-plus-dual automorphism model

The exported construction supplies `CoordinateAction n` for n = 4 or 5,
proves that inverse transpose is noninner and the inner subgroup has index two,
and identifies the actual component layer with that subgroup. The canonical
inner equivalence and the projective/linear automorphism comparison retain
conjugation compatibility.

This discharges the action-existence and group-model inputs for H.9.1; the
quadratic-form, orbit, arbitrary-source-module, and Sylow conclusions are
assembled by their respective consumers.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), printed pp.389–390.
-/
